00:01:01.244 --> 00:01:02.021
- [Voiceover] Matthew asks,

00:01:02.021 --> 00:01:04.855
"You said Pinterest and Twitter
speak different languages.

00:01:04.855 --> 00:01:06.560
"Is it wrong to have my Pinterest account

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:09.161
"tied to my Twitter account
so when I post to Pinterest

00:01:09.161 --> 00:01:11.332
"It auto-posts to Twitter?"

00:01:11.332 --> 00:01:12.620
- Yes, Matthew.

00:01:13.317 --> 00:01:16.143
It is wrong, but it's not super wrong.

00:01:16.143 --> 00:01:18.391
You know, automation has a part

00:01:18.391 --> 00:01:20.272
where, you know, I continue to test

00:01:20.272 --> 00:01:22.175
what's scalable, what's not.

00:01:22.175 --> 00:01:24.416
The reason it's probably wrong is

00:01:24.416 --> 00:01:26.563
you'd probably get a lot more value

00:01:27.032 --> 00:01:29.795
and we all do it, I do it, I
continue to test the wrong way

00:01:29.795 --> 00:01:31.559
to make sure about the right way.

00:01:31.559 --> 00:01:33.475
For example yesterday I put, you know,

00:01:33.475 --> 00:01:34.892
we have started putting out pictures

00:01:34.892 --> 00:01:37.039
that are completely native
to Twitter in the forum.

00:01:37.039 --> 00:01:40.255
Yesterday's photo of me and AJ, you know

00:01:40.255 --> 00:01:42.577
high five surround yourself
with people with permission.

00:01:42.577 --> 00:01:45.073
In the old days, excuse me.

00:01:45.073 --> 00:01:46.512
In the old days

00:01:46.512 --> 00:01:49.252
I would have put the
Instagram link in Twitter.

00:01:49.252 --> 00:01:51.272
And it would have looked like
crap in that crazy screen

00:01:51.272 --> 00:01:52.258
that is Twitter.

00:01:52.258 --> 00:01:53.779
It would have had a link to Instagram.

00:01:53.779 --> 00:01:56.775
You know, Twitter has made
Instagram not native upload.

00:01:56.775 --> 00:01:59.073
And I would have drove
people to that photo.

00:01:59.073 --> 00:02:01.894
But now with the original piece of content

00:02:01.894 --> 00:02:03.298
that got a great engagement.

00:02:03.298 --> 00:02:05.795
Over 100 retweets and favorites yesterday.

00:02:05.795 --> 00:02:09.696
And I accomplished the storytelling
that I wanted on Twitter

00:02:09.696 --> 00:02:11.657
instead of using Twitter as a distribution

00:02:11.657 --> 00:02:12.969
to drive towards Pinterest

00:02:12.969 --> 00:02:16.057
for the added efficiency
that created automation.

00:02:16.057 --> 00:02:17.833
Automation's great

00:02:17.833 --> 00:02:20.028
if you're just trying
to make things happen.

00:02:20.028 --> 00:02:23.034
Meaning like if you're just
trying to get the task done.

00:02:23.034 --> 00:02:25.449
But what about the result
that you're actually trying,

00:02:25.449 --> 00:02:27.735
like why do you tweet?

00:02:27.735 --> 00:02:30.592
You tweet to get your message out.

00:02:30.592 --> 00:02:33.030
And thus, you need to make content native.

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:35.630
So I would say it's wrong.

00:02:35.630 --> 00:02:37.569
Because if you take that same pin,

00:02:37.569 --> 00:02:39.066
whatever you're trying
to achieve on Pinterest,

00:02:39.066 --> 00:02:41.044
and you cropped, what's the crop area,

00:02:41.044 --> 00:02:43.284
we don't, none of the
designers are here, right?

00:02:43.284 --> 00:02:44.736
Dammit, you know.

00:02:44.736 --> 00:02:47.405
If you cropped it
appropriately by default,

00:02:47.405 --> 00:02:50.261
let me, they took my phone too.

00:02:50.261 --> 00:02:52.595
If you cropped it
appropriately it'd do better.

00:02:52.595 --> 00:02:56.085
So the answer is yeah, it's a mistake.

00:02:56.085 --> 00:02:59.626
- Hey Gary, Mottel from Twitter
here and I wanted to ask you

00:02:59.626 --> 00:03:02.342
I have a kosher Latin food
truck at South by Southwest.

00:03:02.342 --> 00:03:04.328
How can I best promote it?

00:03:04.328 --> 00:03:06.603
And how can I get you to
stop by for a free taste

00:03:06.603 --> 00:03:08.809
of some of our great kosher Latin food?

00:03:08.809 --> 00:03:10.945
See you in Austin.

00:03:10.945 --> 00:03:13.289
- You know, the best way
you could promote it is

00:03:13.289 --> 00:03:15.983
to get on the #AskGaryVee Show, check.

00:03:15.983 --> 00:03:18.711
Can I stop by, yes, check.

00:03:18.711 --> 00:03:21.090
It's double check, M!

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:23.308
- Gary, since the robots
seem to be taking over

00:03:23.308 --> 00:03:25.305
in about five years,

00:03:25.305 --> 00:03:27.580
where do you see the role of mankind

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:30.819
in an economy where physical productivity

00:03:30.819 --> 00:03:33.268
isn't really even an issue any more?

00:03:33.268 --> 00:03:36.101
- David, the robots are not
taking over in five years.

00:03:36.101 --> 00:03:36.821
Not even close.

00:03:36.821 --> 00:03:39.827
The robots may take over in 55 years.

00:03:39.827 --> 00:03:41.859
And so since that's so far out,

00:03:41.859 --> 00:03:43.044
I can't wrap my head around it.

00:03:43.044 --> 00:03:45.760
But if the robots take over,

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:48.488
I've got to be really
dead honest with you.

00:03:48.488 --> 00:03:50.520
I'm not worried about the productivity.

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:53.399
I'm scared crapless that
the robots took over.

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:55.639
- Hey Gary, it's DJ Vallauri
from Lodging Interactive.

00:03:55.639 --> 00:03:57.717
My question for you is

00:03:57.717 --> 00:03:59.409
what's your sales process

00:03:59.409 --> 00:04:01.185
when you're working with a prospect?

00:04:01.185 --> 00:04:03.715
How involved are you with your sales team

00:04:03.715 --> 00:04:07.907
in pitching concepts,
ideas, strategies, tac--

00:04:07.907 --> 00:04:09.282
- VJ,

00:04:10.008 --> 00:04:12.132
I'm heavily involved
in getting the client.

00:04:12.132 --> 00:04:14.327
New business pitches
I'm massively involved.

00:04:14.327 --> 00:04:17.445
Our success rate is over
the top with me involved

00:04:17.445 --> 00:04:18.897
compared to me not involved.

00:04:18.897 --> 00:04:21.601
But once they come in, I'm
more on the hunting side.

00:04:21.601 --> 00:04:23.923
On the farming side, I've a lot of SVPs

00:04:23.923 --> 00:04:26.419
high level strategists
who learn the business

00:04:26.419 --> 00:04:28.137
and then are pitching
on a day to day basis.

00:04:28.137 --> 00:04:29.879
Don't forget we, we're
heavy retainer-based

00:04:29.879 --> 00:04:31.678
and then we do incremental above.

00:04:31.678 --> 00:04:34.615
And so the retainer base
kind of takes care of it,

00:04:34.615 --> 00:04:36.327
and then the incrementals added value.

00:04:36.327 --> 00:04:37.906
So there's a little less stress for me

00:04:37.906 --> 00:04:39.368
to make sure that's checked off.

00:04:39.368 --> 00:04:42.131
But the SVPs, the senior
people driving the business,

00:04:42.131 --> 00:04:43.768
are the ones that really are involved

00:04:43.768 --> 00:04:47.455
in the incremental sales
pitch day in and day out.

00:04:47.455 --> 00:04:50.984
And I'm really involved in
up front locking it down.

00:04:50.984 --> 00:04:52.362
And that is a scalable model.

00:04:52.362 --> 00:04:55.299
Because if I do my thing,
and it locks it down

00:04:55.299 --> 00:04:56.483
and creates that base,

00:04:56.483 --> 00:04:58.430
and if I can create it
that it's profitable,

00:04:58.430 --> 00:05:00.554
not that everything is up side after that,

00:05:00.554 --> 00:05:02.168
then that's a good business model.

00:05:02.168 --> 00:05:03.654
- [Voiceover] David asks,
"What are your thoughts

00:05:03.654 --> 00:05:06.805
"on Facebook and their need
to start TV advertising?"

00:05:06.805 --> 00:05:08.929
- David, great question,
and I'm really excited

00:05:08.929 --> 00:05:10.008
about answering this.

00:05:10.008 --> 00:05:11.088
You have to understand
that everything to me

00:05:11.088 --> 00:05:12.342
is an arbitrage.

00:05:12.342 --> 00:05:14.223
So for most businesses in the world

00:05:14.223 --> 00:05:16.944
that don't have complete reach, right?

00:05:16.944 --> 00:05:19.823
TV is not the best value,
hence your hashtag.

00:05:19.823 --> 00:05:22.365
However, for a company
the size of Facebook

00:05:22.365 --> 00:05:25.069
that has reached everybody at some level,

00:05:25.069 --> 00:05:27.345
they've got two places
they can go left, right?

00:05:27.345 --> 00:05:28.919
Which is, and notice it's in the UK.

00:05:28.919 --> 00:05:30.333
They can go, they can go,

00:05:30.333 --> 00:05:32.505
they're struggling a little with 13 to 15

00:05:32.505 --> 00:05:34.792
but they're not going to be
able to market to them on TV.

00:05:34.792 --> 00:05:37.775
I can get them into the pipeline
where Snapchat's winning.

00:05:38.976 --> 00:05:40.973
And then they can go
actually much older, right?

00:05:40.973 --> 00:05:42.633
If you look at the dynamics of, like,

00:05:42.633 --> 00:05:43.794
and this is not much older.

00:05:43.794 --> 00:05:46.476
But if you look at the
dynamics of 70 to 90,

00:05:46.476 --> 00:05:48.739
there's still maybe some upside there.

00:05:48.739 --> 00:05:50.515
And TV has some awareness.

00:05:50.515 --> 00:05:51.862
I think it's overpriced, but when you have

00:05:51.862 --> 00:05:54.312
a market cap of 225 billion,

00:05:54.312 --> 00:05:55.298
that's a hell of a lot more interesting

00:05:55.298 --> 00:05:57.865
to actually do some TV and
have some justification

00:05:57.865 --> 00:06:00.268
over somebody who has a
market cap of 50 billion.

00:06:00.268 --> 00:06:04.141
Or 50 million, or five
million, or 500,000.

00:06:04.141 --> 00:06:04.917
Get it?

00:06:04.917 --> 00:06:07.187
So to me, I can see some justification

00:06:07.187 --> 00:06:08.870
around that tactic.

00:06:08.870 --> 00:06:10.831
You know, it may cost
them a lot more for a user

00:06:10.831 --> 00:06:13.003
but when when you're
left to so little users,

00:06:13.003 --> 00:06:14.384
you've got to pay a lot more.

00:06:14.384 --> 00:06:17.124
Whereas for all of us,
there's so many users left,

00:06:17.124 --> 00:06:20.049
we have to pay as little
as possible to have an ROI.

00:06:20.049 --> 00:06:22.905
Everything is, there is
no one size fits all.

00:06:22.905 --> 00:06:25.366
There is no absolute statements.

00:06:25.366 --> 00:06:27.746
And you've got to make
decisions for your exact moment,

00:06:27.746 --> 00:06:32.123
Facebook television ads in 2005,
'06, '07, '08, '09, '10 eh.

00:06:32.123 --> 00:06:35.664
2015 in the UK market?

00:06:35.664 --> 00:06:36.789
More interesting.

